-- title:
--   Toric-by-finite filtration of Tₚ J_H(M) at p ∥ M
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a level $M \neq 0$ with $p \mid M$ and $p^2 \nmid M$, and a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ containing every unit whose image in $(\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$ is $1$. Assume the $q$-expansion `jqModC ℚ` of $j$ lies in the field `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ ⊤`, and fix: an integral model datum $\mathfrak{X}$ of type `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj`; an automorphism $\theta$ of the geometric function field $\overline{F}_H =$ `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ which, on elements coming from level $M/p$ (for the subgroup `infSubgroup p M H hpM`), acts on Laurent series by the substitution `qExpand (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) p`; a hypothesis `hwgen` saying that $\mathfrak{X}.w$ transports $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points of $\mathfrak{X}$`.Meta.C` in the way matching, under `pointEquivPlace`, the action of $\theta$ on places through `SemilinearAut.ofAlgAut`; a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a non-unit of $A$ and algebraically closed residue field of characteristic $p$, together with a ring map $\rho :$ `R p` $\to A$ compatible with `algebraMap (R p) (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)`; level data $\Lambda$ and a Néron object $O$ of $J_H(M) =$ `Pic0` $(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}, \overline{F}_H)$ at $A$; a hypothesis $hD$ that the designation formed from $O.G$, $O.g$ and the zero section of $O.L$ represents the relative Picard functor cut out by the fibrewise-algebraically-equivalent-to-zero condition `algEquivZeroCut`; the hypothesis that $\Lambda.f$ is smooth and proper with connected fibres and a relative group law; $\Lambda.\sigma_A =$ `Spec.map` of $\rho$; a set $S$ of naturals; and the hypothesis `hinertF` that for every $m > 0$, every $\sigma$ in the inertia subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ and every $m$-torsion class $x$ in `Pic0`, $\sigma \cdot x - x$ lies in $O$`.finPts m`. Then there are $\mathbb{Z}_p$-submodules $T^t, T^f$ of the Tate module $T =$ [`TateModule p (JH M H)`](def/EllipticCurve_TateModule.html#L15) (sequences $(x_n)$ with $p^n x_n = 0$ and $p x_{n+1} = x_n$) such that $x \in T^t$ if and only if $x_n \in O$`.toricPts` $(p^n)$ for all $n$, $x \in T^f$ if and only if $x_n \in O$`.finPts` $(p^n)$ for all $n$ (the latter being generated by the $p^n$-torsion classes whose section extends to the place $A$), with $T^t \le T^f$; both are stable under `tateGenOpH M H S p g` for every Hecke generator $g :$ [`CohCarrier.Gen M S`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L13) and under `JH.tateGaloisRep M H p σ` for every $\sigma$ in the decomposition subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb{Q}$; for $\sigma$ in the inertia subgroup, $\sigma x - x \in T^f$ for all $x \in T$; and for $\sigma$ in the inertia subgroup, $\sigma$ acts on $T^t$ by the scalar `cyclotomicCharacter (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) p σ.toRingEquiv` in $\mathbb{Z}_p$.
--
--   This is the $\ell = p$ case of the monodromy (toric-by-finite) filtration on the $p$-adic Tate module of $J_H(M)$ at a place above $p$ with $p \parallel M$: the toric part carries the cyclotomic character on inertia, the quotient of the finite part by the toric part corresponds to the good-reduction abelian quotient, and no inertia statement is asserted on that middle piece. It feeds the lattice and annihilation arguments used in level lowering, being cited in the degeneracy/Fricke span statement for $T_p J_1$, in the construction of the toric and old lattices, and in the Frobenius–Hecke comparison for $J_0$.
